# PROVENANCE — infinity6e / 0607 / glibc 9.1.0

SigmaStar Alkaid SDK for Infinity6E ("Pudding", vendor CHIP = i6e).
Prebuilt userspace MI libraries. Nothing here is built from source.

## Release

    release_0607   built 2022-06-07 09:41-09:52
    project_commit ceb04c4
    sdk_commit     dc99390
    toolchain      GCC 9.1.0, glibc

The vendor names a drop by its build date, confirmed against two reference
drops: release_0601 = build_time 20220601223756, release_0902 = 20210902165732.
This bundle is six days newer than 0601 and on different commits, so it matches
no public drop exactly.

Read the stamp out of any file with:

    strings libmi_sys.so | grep 'Sigmastar Module'

## Origin

Harvested from a shipped camera firmware and carried via OpenIPC's
sigmastar-osdrv-infinity6e. Not taken from a vendor SDK release tarball --
libmi_sys.so matches neither reference drop by md5, and the set differs both
ways (we carry libcam_*_wrapper, libMD_LINUX, libmi_ive that neither drop has;
we lack libmi_common, libmi_ldc, libmi_vdisp, libsigma3a that both do).

Previously johnchia/sigmastar-sdk @ cdfe9e3e8421dc6929d1e55dce22ab54e7556fd4, under infinity6e/lib/.

